  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Anik Milk Products Pvt. Ltd. vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 4 October, 2019",
    "facts": "Heard on admission as well as I.A.No.18553/2019 which is an application for restraining the arrest of the Officers of the petitioner Company vide Crime No.397/2019 registered at Police Station Sohagpur, District Hoshangabad.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant submits that in view of the provisions of sections 42 and 43 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, the prosecution can be launched on the direction of the Commissioner on complaint under the Food Safety and Standard Act. It is further submitted that so far as other offences under sections 417, 272 and 420 of the I.P.C. are concerned, prima facie they are not made out from the FIR. As there is no cognizable offence, hence, no FIR can be lodged and no investigation can be made.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the applicant submits that in view of the provisions of sections 42 and 43 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, the prosecution can be launched on the direction of the Commissioner on complaint under the Food Safety and Standard Act. It is further submitted that so far as other offences under sections 417, 272 and 420 of the I.P.C. are concerned, prima facie they are not made out from the FIR. As there is no cognizable offence, hence, no FIR can be lodged and no investigation can be made.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
